<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Tudor returns for her subsequent annual wellness visit, a week after her last depression review. She completed the health risk assessment with the nurse beforehand, in a private room at the end of the day as she asked. Her sore throat settled within a week. She takes sertraline 50 mg each morning without side effects and has had four sessions of interpersonal psychotherapy. Her mood is better on most days; she sleeps about five hours, eats three small meals and a supplement a day, and has gained 0.5 kg. Her new partial denture is being made. She has had no falls since the stumble in December and walks in the gardens most days. She has had no emergency visits or hospital stays in the past year. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Subsequent annual wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Major depression improving on sertraline and IPT; insomnia improving with CBT-I; dental work under way</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg; no over-the-counter sleep aids or cold remedies</td></tr><tr><td>Safety events</td><td>No falls since December</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair; better than a month ago</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Grieving the friends she has lost; lonely at times despite a full household; she has begun seeing two old friends again</td></tr><tr><td>Behavioral</td><td>Never smoker; a small glass of wine some evenings; walks 20 to 30 minutes most days; meals small but regular</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in bathing, dressing, eating, toileting, and transfers</td></tr><tr><td>Instrumental activities of daily living</td><td>Manages her own affairs and papers; her staff run the household</td></tr><tr><td>Home safety</td><td>Stairs with rails; rugs taped down after the home review; night lights in the bedroom and hallway; smoke detectors working</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears well; reading glasses; eye examination last year</td></tr><tr><td>Bladder</td><td>No leakage</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>No concerns; MoCA 27 in January</td></tr><tr><td>Pain</td><td>An occasional ache in the right shoulder; no other pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

