    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Subsequent annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the personalized prevention plan updated; a written copy was given to her in person. Depression is under treatment, the cognitive screen in January was normal, and fall risk is moderate because of low weight, an SSRI, and last year&apos;s fall. [S]<list><item>Next annual wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder (F32.1)</content>. PHQ-9 11, down from 17 at intake; improving but not yet a response. No suicidal thoughts. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg and IPT; depression review in two weeks as planned.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Fall risk (Z91.81)</content>. No falls since December; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; home changes made. [S]<list><item>Continue the balance and strength class twice a week.</item><item>DXA of the hip and spine ordered: she is 69, with low body weight and a fall in the past year.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Up to date</td><td>High-dose vaccine in October</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PCV20 three years ago; no further doses needed</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two-dose series completed five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap seven years ago</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No chronic heart or lung disease or other condition that raises her risk; to be offered at 75</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 11 while under treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 27 seven weeks ago; no concerns from her or her staff</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One fall last year; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; exercise class and home review in place</td></tr><tr><td>Osteoporosis screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>DXA ordered; recommended for women 65 or older</td></tr><tr><td>Breast cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Mammogram ten months ago, normal; every two years to 74</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Colonoscopy four years ago, normal</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Over 65 with adequate normal screening before</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol misuse screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C 1</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>One-time test done before, negative</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Whispered-voice test passed; eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: COVID-19 vaccine, 1602-1603 formula [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Depression review in two weeks as planned. DXA in the next month. Next annual wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1603-03-16: seven-week depression treatment review. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
